#: 31de8e4770e24a3886a84156f669c61b
msgid "Reference"
msgstr ""

#: 6f88c62da7244c1ca9cd01d433855fd8
msgid "Reference guides are **technical descriptions** of the machinery and how to operate it. Reference material is **information-oriented**."
msgstr ""

#: 281b1196b2c14d3880cdb8df5a95c0f9
msgid "Reference material contains *propositional or theoretical* knowledge that a user looks to in their *work*."
msgstr ""

#: e879f67a69af4e7084e49a6bdf6f0755
msgid "The only purpose of a reference guide is to describe, as succinctly as possible, and in an orderly way. Whereas the content of tutorials and how-to guides are led by needs of the user, reference material is led by the product it describes."
msgstr ""

#: b7f13349eb2c4125bc0bc721a2b4cac3
msgid "Reference - information oriented, theoretical knowledge, that serves our work"
msgstr ""

#: cd7c0bbaa008401a9e7a642d355edeab
msgid "In the case of software, reference guides describe the software itself - APIs, classes, functions and so on - and how to use them."
msgstr ""

#: d45ef664b1704313b9f22dd28182af29
msgid "Your users need reference material because they need truth and certainty - firm platforms on which to stand while they work. Good technical reference is essential to provide users with the confidence to do their work."
msgstr ""

#: 6c2bda2f5cd647538286bf1612749597
msgid "Reference as description"
msgstr ""

#: d49c8462f2174935ab32b27a2ddb25d8
msgid "Reference material describes the machinery. It should be **austere**. One hardly *reads* reference material; one *consults* it."
msgstr ""

#: 4bda532e38734a2994a767c06882de7a
msgid "There should be no doubt or ambiguity in reference; it should be wholly authoritative."
msgstr ""

#: feb94a87c6eb42598a501fc0f06ab1e4
msgid "Reference material is like a map. A map tells you what you need to know about the territory, without having to go out and check the territory for yourself; a reference guide serves the same purpose for the product and its internal machinery."
msgstr ""

#: 35bb3f2baec74abe9847ffc0c0930a42
msgid "Although reference should not attempt to show how to perform tasks, it can and often needs to include a description of how something works or the correct way to use it."
msgstr ""

#: 6e9a5d9bf60246138827ad753e99a613
msgid "Unfortunately, too many software developers think that auto-generated reference material is all the documentation required."
msgstr ""

#: efc99c1b51ee44cb8fed9b8cc974e658
msgid "Some reference material (such as API documentation) can be generated automatically by the software it describes, which is a powerful way of ensuring that it remains faithfully accurate to the code."
msgstr ""

#: 3e94eee9686749cf89fe15e5ea2cb46e
msgid "Key principles"
msgstr ""

#: e561f87fe3c4488d9d57b9a666f7f96d
msgid "Describe and only describe"
msgstr ""

#: 3dbd04572d204de4bb3ea0af2667d198
msgid "*Neutral description* is the key imperative of technical reference."
msgstr ""

#: 42c0daf4da7746cf86c37173c2729426
msgid "austere and uncompromising"
msgstr ""

#: 4bd339875b1942a892fb960820d665f0
msgid "neutrality, objectivity, factuality"
msgstr ""

#: 042f651aa418417cb4b586e495968c3e
msgid "structured according to the structure of the machinery itself"
msgstr ""

#: 7c721fa196a9423ea8e88f1450c70cfa
msgid "Unfortunately one of the hardest things to do is to describe something neutrally. It's not a natural way of communicating. What's natural on the other hand is to explain, instruct, discuss, opine, and all these things run counter to the needs of technical reference, which instead demands accuracy, precision, completeness and clarity."
msgstr ""

#: 0c956537733b445ba9dfdf8664508128
msgid "It can be tempting to introduce instruction and explanation, simply because description can seem too inadequate to be useful, and because we do indeed need these other things. Instead, link to how-to guides, explanation and introductory tutorials."
msgstr ""

#: 8e3e23b151494501966064a49fcd488c
msgid "Adopt standard patterns"
msgstr ""

#: c35a094ac80b4f5dbf46b7f33e339c52
msgid "**Reference material is useful when it is consistent.** Standard patterns are what allow us to use reference material effectively. Your job is to place the material that your user needs where they expect to find it, in a format that they are familiar with."
msgstr ""

#: d901750157e142f98d41ae84c643ad23
msgid "There are many opportunities in writing to delight your readers with your extensive vocabulary and command of multiple styles, but reference material is definitely not one of them."
msgstr ""

#: 55dc7cf5848a4239a2746c2b09bbaa20
msgid "Respect the structure of the machinery"
msgstr ""

#: 032a7d13dcc649f5ad7455e4cabc2802
msgid "The way a map corresponds to the territory it represents helps us use the former to find our way through the latter. It should be the same with documentation: **the structure of the documentation should mirror the structure of the product**, so that the user can work their way through them at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: fed009fc4f554a3ba4f551c9367cad59
msgid "It doesn't mean forcing the documentation into an unnatural structure. What's important is that the logical, conceptual arrangement of and relations within the code should help make sense of the documentation."
msgstr ""

#: 016528e932b042308c950a5c3d6b3fa1
msgid "Provide examples"
msgstr ""

#: 13a0cd84765a4876b1e2307f8f48516b
msgid "**Examples** are valuable ways of providing illustration that helps readers understand reference, while avoiding the risk of becoming distracted from the job of describing. For example, an example of usage of a command can be a succinct way of illustrating it and its context, without falling into the trap of trying to explain or instruct."
msgstr ""

#: edbe885868644b2184840f485f2581fe
msgid "The language of reference guides"
msgstr ""

#: b90551c0ed91442db026ea02d4b81d62
msgid "Django's default logging configuration inherits Python's defaults. It's available as ``django.utils.log.DEFAULT_LOGGING`` and defined in ``django/utils/log.py``"
msgstr ""

#: 249ef6ab454d47aea056f61a9d0f187b
msgid "State facts about the machinery and its behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: 4dd7e45cf39144d8ab1d8a3180b227e5
msgid "Sub-commands are: a, b, c, d, e, f."
msgstr ""

#: 8fe2e9b25be54e3c85b152fe1a78d72e
msgid "List commands, options, operations, features, flags, limitations, error messages, etc."
msgstr ""

#: b7419627f0fb48f59b7cd5630947f043
msgid "You must use a. You must not apply b unless c. Never d."
msgstr ""

#: 2948cf2ef0174086b8ea9050cbf6e463
msgid "Provide warnings where appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: 50932cfeba164161bd83d1eaa6e2830a
msgid "Applied to food and cooking"
msgstr ""

#: c9e069deef41442cb17352fdcf642145
msgid "You might check the information on a packet of food, in order to help you make a decision about what to do."
msgstr ""

#: 0863acc9c2ab441b8dbdac044921cc08
msgid "When you're looking for information - relevant facts - you do not want to be confronted by opinions, speculation, instructions or interpretation."
msgstr ""

#: 9910712cd98e4385b73f0a520bb4907a
msgid "Information on the back of a packet of lasagne"
msgstr ""

#: ddfe41281463483497959bf09902efe5
msgid "You also expect that information to be presented in standard ways, so that you - when you need to know about something's nutritional properties, how it should be stored, its ingredients, what health implications it might have - can find them quickly, and know you can rely on them."
msgstr ""

#: 10170d09575b4a2b98f297ef101a916c
msgid "So you expect to see for example: *May contain traces of wheat*. Or: *Net weight: 1000g*."
msgstr ""

#: 6b342ed39bf3482f8d604949deaa3614
msgid "You will certainly not expect to find for example recipes or marketing claims mixed up with this information; that could be literally dangerous."
msgstr ""

#: 19c5a268d8df407c95d660d58a689226
msgid "The way reference material is presented on food products is so important that it's usually governed by law, and the same kind of seriousness should apply to all reference documentation."
msgstr ""
